Title: Is passing pointer to an array as pointer to pointer UB in C?.
Body: <p>I have such a code:</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;

void func(int **b)
{
    printf(&quot;b = %p\n&quot;, b); // 0x7ffe76932330
    *b = *b + 1;
}

int main(void)
{
