Title: Repeat animation from the beginning every time the element comes into view.
Body: <p>I have created an animation that takes a couple of seconds to play. The animation should only run when the element is in view, so I've used <code>whileInView</code>. This works correctly, but when I scroll down (so the element is out of view), the animation seems to run backwards, because when I scroll up again, I can see that the animation does not start from the beginning but from the point that it reached when it ran backwards and when the element came into view again. I want the animation to run from the beginning instead.</p>
<p>I've created a small sandbox to demonstrate the issue:</p>
<p><a href="https://codesandbox.io/s/dreamy-cache-mk2dq2?file=/src/App.js" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codesandbox.io/s/dreamy-cache-mk2dq2?file=/src/App.js</a></p>
<pre><code>import &quot;./styles.css&quot;;
import { motion } from &quot;framer-motion&quot;;

export default function App() {
  return (
    &lt;div style={{ height: &quot;1000px&quot; }}&gt;
      &lt;motion.div
        id=&quot;box&quot;
        initial={{ x: 0 }}
        whileInView={{ x: 300 }}
        transition={{ duration: 5, ease: &quot;linear&quot; }}
      &gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
          The box should be moving now. Scroll down and then up again. The
          animation will not instantly reset but run backwards.
        &lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;/motion.div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
