Title: Flutter submit data to http.post timeout issue.
Body: <p>I have a flutter app where data is submitted via http.post to a php/mysql server.  The data is then inserted into the database.  Usually everything works fine and I have a timeout built in where if the time is exceeded it returns a &quot;could not connect&quot; error back to the flutter client.</p>
<p>Occasionally though, the app times out but the data is still submitted and inserted.  I'm thinking that the data posted to the server but for whatever reason a response was not received back in time.</p>
<p>Looking for help or ideas on how maybe to make my code better to deal with this issue other then just increasing the timeout.  Thanks.</p>
<pre><code>postData() async {
    const url = 'https://www.testdomain.com/app/submit.php';
    try {
      final response = await http.post(Uri.parse(url), body: {
        &quot;id&quot;: user,
        &quot;notes&quot;: notesController.text
      }).timeout(const Duration(seconds: 4), onTimeout: () {
        //Time has run out
        return http.Response('Error', 408);
      });
      if (response.statusCode == 408) {
        if (!mounted) return;
        setState(() {
          status = '1';
        });
      } else if (response.statusCode == 200) {
        final auth = json.decode(response.body);
        if (!mounted) return;
        setState(() {
          success = auth[0]['success'].toString();
          status = auth[0]['status'].toString();
        });
      } else {
        if (!mounted) return;
        setState(() {
          status = '1';
        });
      }
    } catch (e) {
      if (!mounted) return;
      setState(() {
        status = '1';
      });
    }
}
</code></pre>

