Title: QTableView event filter not detecting some mouse events.
Body: <p>I installed a custom event filter to a TableView :</p>
<pre><code>ui-&gt;groupBox-&gt;getView()-&gt;installEventFilter(mEventHandler.get());
</code></pre>
<p>and here is (part of) the eventFilter implementation :</p>
<pre><code>bool EventHandler::eventFilter(QObject *watched, QEvent *event)
{
    if (event-&gt;type() == QEvent::ToolTip)
    {
        return handleTooltipEvent(watched, event);
    }
    else if (event-&gt;type() == QEvent::MouseButtonPress)
    {
        return handleMouseClickEvent(watched, event);
    }
    ...

}
</code></pre>
<p>But the MouseEvents never arrive at the eventFilter. I did a step by step debug, all types of events come through here but no mouse related event. When I click, the events arriving here are <code>QEvent::InputMethodQuery</code> events.</p>
