  box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px currentColor, 0 0px 15px 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  border-radius: 50%;
  transition: 0.8s;
}

#spin::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: -17px;
  border: 10px solid transparent;
  border-bottom-color: currentColor;
  border-top: none;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="wheelOfFortune"&gt;
  &lt;canvas id="wheel" width="300" height="300"&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;
  &lt;div id="spin"&gt;SPIN&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>That's what I'm trying to do
<a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/TLmzK.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/TLmzK.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>Solution: <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5026961/html5-canvas-ctx-filltext-wont-do-line-breaks">HTML5 canvas ctx.fillText won&#39;t do line breaks?</a></p>
