Title: Issue in overriding color-scheme of iframe.
Body: <p>I'm developing website, which using an iframe to show a 3rd party html page and this page has some minimal prefers-color-scheme CSS media queries to switch between light or dark colour background (code shown below).</p>
<p><strong>I want:</strong></p>
<p>In my application, I'm not using any light/dark theme and <strong>want show 3rd party html page (in Iframe) always in light theme irrespective of OS dark/light mode settings</strong> (I'm using Mac OS Ventura in dark mode + Chrome 111.0).</p>
<p><strong>Problem:</strong></p>
<p>I've tried multiple ways to achieve this including <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/65260505/disqus-iframe-transparency-wont-work-on-chrome-87/65313819#65313819">link-1</a> and <a href="https://sergeyski.com/css-color-scheme-and-iframes-lessons-learned-from-disqus-background-bug/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">link-2</a>, unfortunately didn't work well, getting iframe in dark mode.</p>
<p>I've explored other stackoverflow Q&amp;A's as well, but many of them  utilising <em>color-schema meta tags</em>, which is not viable in my case.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!--  My html page, which embedding the 3rd party html page in iframe. --&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
  figure {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.5em;
    margin: 1em 0;
    border: thin dashed gray;
    /* experiment-1 adding to the parent element */
    color-scheme: light;
    color-scheme: only light;
  }

  iframe {
    width: 100%;
    height: 10em;
    background-color: white;
  }
  /* want to show iframe always in light mode*/
   :root {
    color-scheme: light;
    color-scheme: only light;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    /* want to show iframe always in light mode*/
    iframe#test {
      color-scheme: light;
      color-scheme: only light;
    }
  }
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Iframe src with always-light mode wanted&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;figure&gt;
  &lt;iframe id="test" src="http://localhost:8000/iframe.html"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!--  3rd party html page, contains media query for color scheme,
 and displays bg/color based on it--&gt;

&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;

&lt;html&gt;
  &lt;head&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --bg-color: #0a0524;
          --main-color: #fff;
        }
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
        :root {
          --bg-color: #fff;
          --main-color: #0a0524;
        }
      }
      :root {
        color: var(--main-color);
        background-color: var(--bg-color);
      }
    &lt;/style&gt;
  &lt;/head&gt;

  &lt;body&gt;
    &lt;b&gt;
      &lt;p&gt;Some heading&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Important Information&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Important Information para&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/GIjlH.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/GIjlH.png" alt="Always ignoring Iframe's color-scheme, and using OS Settings via prefers-color-scheme media query" /></a></p>
<p>As shown in above picture, chrome is always ignoring Iframe's <code>color-scheme:light</code> set by parent, and applying <code>@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark)</code> media-query.</p>
<p>Please note, My OS is <strong>running in dark mode</strong> (Mac OS Ventura, Chrome Version 111.0).</p>
<p><strong>My question</strong> is how I can forcefully apply CSS color-scheme to iframe from parent?</p>
<p>Please share your thoughts. Any suggestions/comments are also welcome.</p>
<p>Thanking you in advance.</p>

Title: Button not clickable over iframe on mobile web.
Body: <p>I am attempting to place a button absolutely <em>over</em> an iframe. When viewing my app in mobile web, however, no button click is registered; iInstead, a click is registered on the iframe that's <em>underneath</em> it.</p>
<p>The exact same implementation works on non-mobile web.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/w4yu2.png" alt="Here is a picture of the implementation for visualization purposes" /></p>
<p>Here is the code I am currently using:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div style={{ width: '100vw', height: '100vh', display: 'flex', position: 'relative' }} /&gt;
   &lt;button
      style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, bottom: 0, zIndex: 1  }}
      onClick={() =&gt; console.log('button clicked')}
   &gt;
      click here
   &lt;/button&gt;

   &lt;iframe style={{ width: '100%' }} src={src} /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>A few other things I have tried:</p>
<ul>
<li>Setting the <code>z-index</code> of the <code>iframe</code> to a lower number (<code>iframe</code> still gets clicked)</li>
<li>Disabling <code>pointer-events</code> on the <code>iframe</code> (the button click is still not registered)</li>
<li>Wrapping the <code>button</code> in a <code>div</code></li>
<li>Wrapping the <code>iframe</code> in a <code>div</code></li>
<li>Stopping propagation of the click event of the <code>button</code></li>
</ul>

