Title: SwiftUI Charts BarMark Foreground Style Color Based on Fixed Values.
Body: <p>I'm trying to format the color of a BarMark in SwiftUI Charts where the color is
determined by a fixed value definition. Say there is a data element with a high of 162 and
a low of -10. I want the bar color from any negative number to 0 to be blue, from 0 to 35
to be green, from 35 to 70 to be yellow, from 70 to 105 to be orange and anything
over 105 to be red.</p>
<p>This is how I want it to look.</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/nyhHw.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/nyhHw.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>I achieved this by creating 5 records and listing the
high and low for each segment. My input data will only give me the bar high and low i.e.
162 and -10 in this example. I tried to create an IF structure to calculate the high
and low values from the given data, but it quickly becomes a nightmare once you take
into account that the data high and low could be anything as long as high &gt;= low.</p>
<p>Here's the code for the above view:</p>
<pre><code>struct ContentView: View {

    var yValues: [Int] {
        stride(from: -35, to: 210, by: 35).map { $0 }
    }

    let stackColors: [Color] = [.red, .orange, .yellow, .green, .blue]

    var body: some View {
        VStack{
            Chart(revenueDataRule) { item in
                    BarMark(
                        x: .value(&quot;Period&quot;, item.period),
                        //y: .value(&quot;Amount&quot;, item.amount)
                        yStart: .value(&quot;High&quot;, item.high),
                        yEnd: .value(&quot;Low&quot;, item.low),
                        width: 20
                    )
                    .foregroundStyle(by: .value(&quot;Department&quot;, item.band))
