Title: C++ hash_map find() vs contains() performance.
Body: <p>What's the better option performance-wise if I want to check if an element is contained in a map and use it directly afterwards?</p>
<pre><code>std::unordered_map&lt;int, std::string&gt; my_map;
int my_key;
</code></pre>
<p>Option 1:</p>
<pre><code>if (const auto&amp; iter = my_map.find(my_key); iter != my_map.end()) {
      const auto&amp; value = iter-&gt;second;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Option 2:</p>
<pre><code>if (my_map.contains(my_key)) {
      const auto&amp; value = my_map.at(my_key);
}
</code></pre>
<p>For readability I prefer option 2. However, from my understanding Option 2 should be slower since there are two hashmap lookups.</p>

Title: C++ doesn&#39;t convert the uppercase &quot;I&quot; character to lowercase correctly.
Body: <p>I have this simple C++ code that converts uppercase characters to lowercase:</p>
