Title: recommendation engine with apache couch-db and nano: filter a view for a specific user.
Body: <p>I'm building a recommendation system for a webshop. The shopping history is saved in a couch-db database. I'm creating a view through map-reduce that emits for each user and product, the quantity of that product bought. The reduce parts consists in taking the sum.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>// map 
const onCheckout = (doc) =&gt; {
  const { username, items } = doc;

  // once a checkout is done (i.e. history db is populated)
  // map every items bought
  items.map((item) =&gt; emit([username, item.name], item.quantity));
};
</code></pre>
<p>I can then fetch my recommendation service and grab the view.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>router.get(&quot;/recommendation/user&quot;, jwt, (req, res) =&gt; {
  const { username } = req.auth;
  history
    .view(&quot;on-checkout__user&quot;, &quot;items_bought&quot;, {
      group: true,
    })
    .then((body) =&gt; {
      console.log(body.rows);
      res.status(200).json({ content: body.rows });
    })
    .catch((err) =&gt; res.send(err));
});
</code></pre>
<p>This gives me the following results
<a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/UmcZY.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/UmcZY.png" alt="view" /></a></p>
<p>The first key is the username, then the product. The value is the total quantity of that product bought by the user. However, I would like the filter that view only for a specific user (the one that makes the request with a JWT in the headers, e.g. only for the user called &quot;potiron&quot;). I know I can pass a key in the parameters of the view function, I tried with <code>{key: &quot;potiron&quot;}</code> but it does not work. Is there any other way ?</p>

Title: Hive INSERT OVERWRITE creates 1 large file in every partition.
Body: <p>I am executing a hive INSERT OVERWRITE query.</p>
<pre><code>SET hive.merge.mapredfiles=false;
