Title: What is the proper procedure for working with multiple channels in netty?.
Body: <p>I have a UDP Multicast application which will be hardcoded to listen to specific groups of multicasts addresses. However, while I am able to have one NioDatagramChannel that joins multiple groups, my code cannot handle multiple NioDatagramChannels that listens to separate groups (somewhat like Java NIO selector). The following is the code I wrote:</p>
<pre><code>public class NettyTest implements Runnable {
    public static void main(String[] args){
        new NettyTest().run();
    }
    @Override
    public void run() {
        MulticastHandler handler = new MulticastHandler();
        MulticastHandler handler2 = new MulticastHandler();
        EventLoopGroup group = new NioEventLoopGroup();
        try{
            UDPChannel channel = new UDPChannel(5555, &quot;eth0&quot;, &quot;239.1.1.1&quot;);
            UDPChannel channel2 = new UDPChannel(5556, &quot;eth0&quot;, &quot;225.1.1.1&quot;);

            Bootstrap b = new Bootstrap();
            NetworkInterface ni = NetworkInterface.getByName(&quot;eth0&quot;);
            b.group(group)
                    .channel(NioDatagramChannel.class)
                    .option(ChannelOption.SO_REUSEADDR, true)
                    .option(ChannelOption.IP_MULTICAST_IF, ni)
                    .option(ChannelOption.SO_RCVBUF, 1500 * 200)
                    .handler(new ChannelInitializer&lt;NioDatagramChannel&gt;() {
                        @Override
                        protected void initChannel(NioDatagramChannel nioDatagramChannel) throws Exception {
                            nioDatagramChannel.pipeline().addLast(new MulticastHandler());  //&lt;------------- modification
                        }
                    });

            System.out.println(channel.getMULTICAST_STRING()+&quot; &quot;+channel2.getMULTICAST_STRING());

            AttributeKey&lt;String&gt; markerKey = AttributeKey.valueOf(&quot;Marker&quot;);
            NioDatagramChannel ch = (NioDatagramChannel)b.bind(5555).sync().channel();
            ch.attr(markerKey).set(channel.getMULTICAST_STRING());
            ch.joinGroup(new InetSocketAddress(&quot;239.1.1.1&quot;, 5555), ni).sync();
            group.register(ch);

            NioDatagramChannel ch1 =(NioDatagramChannel)b.bind(5556).sync().channel();
            ch1.attr(markerKey).set(channel2.getMULTICAST_STRING());
            ch1.joinGroup(new InetSocketAddress(&quot;225.1.1.1&quot;, 5556), ni).sync();
            group.register(ch1);

//            ch.closeFuture().await();
//            ch1.closeFuture().await();
            ch.closeFuture();
            ch1.closeFuture();
        } catch (InterruptedException | SocketException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}

class MulticastHandler extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler&lt;DatagramPacket&gt;{
    private MoldUdpHeader moldUdpHeader = new MoldUdpHeader();
    AttributeKey&lt;String&gt; markerKey = AttributeKey.valueOf(&quot;Marker&quot;);
    @Override
    protected void channelRead0(ChannelHandlerContext channelHandlerContext, DatagramPacket datagramPacket) throws Exception {
        moldUdpHeader.decode(datagramPacket.content().nioBuffer(), 0);
        System.out.println(channelHandlerContext.channel().attr(markerKey).get()+&quot; &quot;+moldUdpHeader.getSeqNum());
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>I have tried the above but it gives a <code>io.netty.channel.StacklessClosedChannelException at io.netty.channel.AbstractChannel$AbstractUnsafe.ensureOpen(ChannelPromise)(Unknown Source)</code>. What is the proper way to be able to process both of these channels? I do not want to combine both into one channel, because the messages on both channels can have same ID but different values (values are specific for that channel).</p>
