Title: Number of wires in a ZKP Circom circuit is greater than expected.
Body: <p>I compile this simple circuit:</p>
<pre><code>pragma circom 2.0.0;

template Multiplier2() {
    signal input a;
    signal input b;
    signal output c;
    c &lt;== a*b;
 }

 component main = Multiplier2();
</code></pre>
<p>and the compiler says 4 wires:</p>
<pre><code>circom 1.circom --r1cs --wasm --sym --c
template instances: 1
non-linear constraints: 1
linear constraints: 0
public inputs: 0
public outputs: 1
private inputs: 2
private outputs: 0
wires: 4
labels: 4
</code></pre>
<p>I have expected that the number of wires will be the number of signals (3), I wonder where the 4th wire comes from?</p>

