% J(w,b) =(y-y_est)^2

w = 0;
b = 0;
alpha =.000001; % I tried various alphas like 0.01, .1 etc. (Not working)
for i =1: 100
    y_est = w*x + b;
    J = mean((y-y_est).^2)
    temp_w = w + alpha*(mean(x.*(y-w*x-b)));
    temp_b = b + alpha*(mean(y-w*x-b));
    w =temp_w
    b =temp_b
end
</code></pre>
<p>For some reason, it is not working. It seems like my algorithm is not converging.</p>
