Title: Layout returning wrong keys in custom keyboard Android jetpack compose.
Body: <p>I'm facing an issue with my Android Compose keyboard layout where the symbol layout is displaying the &quot;qwerty&quot; label instead of the expected symbols. I've tried troubleshooting, but I can't seem to figure out what's causing this problem. Here are the details:</p>
<p>I have implemented a custom Android Compose keyboard with two layout states: &quot;qwerty&quot; and &quot;symbols.&quot; The idea is to switch between these layouts to input either regular text or symbols.</p>
<p>When I switch to the &quot;symbols&quot; layout and press a key, it correctly displays the symbol character on the key itself, but the character entered into the text field is still the &quot;qwerty&quot; character, which is unexpected.</p>
<p>I've verified that the layout state switches correctly to &quot;symbols&quot; when the layout switch key is pressed.</p>
<p>In the symbolsLayout array, I've defined the symbol characters I want to display for each key.</p>
<p>The CustomKey composable, which handles key presses, seems to be aware of the currentLayout state to determine whether to display symbols or qwerty characters.</p>
<p>Here is my code.
